HCMS DEV API DOCUMENTATION

Authentication



====> Register patient account
Method: POST
URL: http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/register
JSON: {
  "email": "patient@example.com",
  "password": "secure-password"
}

RESPONSE: {
  "accessToken": "jwt-token",
  "tokenType": "Bearer",
  "expiresIn": 3600,
  "user": {
    "id": 1,
    "email": "patient@example.com",
    "role": "PATIENT",
    "enabled": true,
    "createdAt": "2026-09-01T16:00:00Z"
  }
}

New public registrations always receive the PATIENT role.


====> Login
Method: POST
URL: http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/login
JSON: {
  "email": "patient@example.com",
  "password": "secure-password"
}

RESPONSE: {
  "accessToken": "jwt-token",
  "tokenType": "Bearer",
  "expiresIn": 3600,
  "user": {
    "id": 1,
    "email": "patient@example.com",
    "role": "PATIENT",
    "enabled": true,
    "createdAt": "2026-09-01T16:00:00Z"
  }
}

Use the token for protected endpoints.
Headers: {
  "Authorization": "Bearer <accessToken>"
}


User Management



====> Create user
Method: POST
URL: http://localhost:8080/api/v1/users
JSON: {
  "email": "patient@example.com",
  "password": "secure-password",
  "role": "PATIENT"
}

RESPONSE: {
  "id": 1,
  "email": "patient@example.com",
  "role": "PATIENT",
  "enabled": true,
  "createdAt": "2026-09-01T16:00:00Z"
}


======> Get all users
Method: GET
URL: http://localhost:8080/api/v1/users?page=0&size=20

RESPONSE: {
  "content": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "email": "patient@example.com",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "enabled": true,
      "createdAt": "2026-09-01T16:00:00Z"
    }
  ],
  "totalElements": 1,
  "totalPages": 1,
  "size": 20,
  "number": 0
}


=====> Get user by id
Method: GET
URL: http://localhost:8080/api/v1/users/:id

RESPONSE: {
  "id": 1,
  "email": "patient@example.com",
  "role": "PATIENT",
  "enabled": true,
  "createdAt": "2026-09-01T16:00:00Z"
}


=====> Update user by id
Method: PUT
URL: http://localhost:8080/api/v1/users/:id
JSON: {
  "email": "new-email@example.com",
  "password": "new-secure-password",
  "role": "RECEPTIONIST",
  "enabled": true
}

You can send only the fields you want to update.


=====> Delete user by id
Method: DELETE
URL: http://localhost:8080/api/v1/users/:id
RESPONSE: 204 No Content


User roles

ADMIN
DOCTOR
RECEPTIONIST
PATIENT


Errors

400 - Invalid request data
404 - User not found
409 - Email already exists


Run application

./mvnw spring-boot:run


Database configuration

DB_PORT default is 5433
DB_NAME default is hcms
DB_USER default is hcms_user
DB_PASSWORD default is hcms_pass


User management endpoints require an ADMIN token.
